Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Second of two consecutive patches closing the 'Known Gaps' (patch 4
was the data layer; this is route wiring that consumes it).

Route changes:
- candidates DELETE -> requirePermission('candidates', 'delete')
- job-postings DELETE/close -> requirePermission('job_postings', 'delete'/'close')
- applications list/get/create -> requirePermission('applications', 'read'/'write');
  stage-transition endpoints (advance/block/hold) moved from the old
  overloaded 'workflow' key to 'workflow_actions'
- workflow (templates) -> requirePermission('workflow', 'read'/'write'),
  now safe since manager/hr hold 'read' post-patch-4
- performance strategies -> requirePermission('strategy', 'read'/'write')
- credits top-up/adjust -> requirePermission('credit_account', 'write'/'adjust')
- organizations list/get/update/modules -> requirePermission('organisations', 'read'/'write')

The last two land real restriction without needing a separate
platform-admin login flow: requirePermission just reads whatever
roles are embedded in the caller's JWT, so as soon as a platform_admin
user exists these are properly locked to them. Provisioning that first
platform_admin user is still manual (direct user_team_role insert,
team_id NULL) — flagged as a next step, not solved here.

Also fixes a real bug: requirePermission threw 401 Unauthorized on a
failed permission check. Wrong status — the caller IS authenticated,
they just lack the permission — so it now throws 403 Forbidden.
requireAuth (missing/invalid token) still correctly returns 401.

walkthrough.md updated: 'Known Gaps' section rewritten to show what's
resolved vs. what's still open (platform_admin provisioning is now
the main remaining item).

Tests: 22/22 passing. Added coverage specifically proving the gap
closures: applications requires auth, GET /organizations is 403 for
org_admin but 200-track for platform_admin (confirms the permission
actually discriminates correctly rather than just being present).
